    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nMap\r\n\r\n### Description\r\nFirst of all - thank you so much for this amazing project and I am really devastated I did not find it earlier, it could've save me days of time.\r\nI am experimenting with map symbols but it appear to not take effect and I have no idea why.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_20240410_132012](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/22867443/ed218707-6c8e-459f-9c8f-52871786ab27)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>config</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\nlocal minimap = require(\"mini.map\")\r\nminimap.setup {\r\n    {\r\n        symbols = {\r\n            -- Scrollbar parts for view and line. Use empty string to disable any.\r\n            -- - Line - '🮚', '▶'.\r\n            -- - View - '╎', '┋', '┋'.\r\n            -- scroll_line = '█',\r\n            -- scroll_view = '┃',\r\n            -- scroll_line = '..',\r\n            -- scroll_view = '.',\r\n            scroll_line = '▶',\r\n            scroll_view = '┋',\r\n        },\r\n        window = {\r\n            show_integration_count = true,\r\n            width = 7,\r\n            winblend = 25,\r\n            zindex = 10,\r\n        },\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nmap symbols are updated on nvim restart\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\ndefault symbols are used after relaunch",
